 updates, decides when to stop and picks the best candidate, solving Sudoku-Extreme with 1.8M parameters."},{"id":"2611.09894","date":"2026-11-09","title":"Video-Coder: Reinforcing Agentic Coding for Video Generation","tldr":"Video-Coder trains a coding agent to build a 3D draft scene in Blender, which guides a video generator and raises physical plausibility scores on two benchmarks."},{"id":"2611.03634","date":"2026-11-07","title":"WebHarbor: Docking Real Websites for Evolving GUI Agent Environments","tldr":"WebHarbor rebuilds 153 real websites as offline, resettable Docker environments with 3,518 tasks, and a 4B web agent trained only there matches or beats one trained on live sites."},{"id":"2611.03097","date":"2026-11-04","title":"DR Pixel: Page-Native Deep Research with Vision-Language Models","tldr":"DR Pixel does deep research directly on rendered page images instead of OCR text, and a step-weighted fine-tuning method lifts a 27B open model to GPT-5.4-level accuracy."},{"id":"2610.42149","date":"2026-11-02","title":"Latent Reasoning in Continuous Space for Unified Multimodal Models","tldr":"LARC lets a unified image model think in continuous hidden states instead of text before drawing, trained with a curriculum and a self-supervised information-gain reward, and it improves with more thinking."},{"id":"2610.38681","date":"2026-10-30","title":"Weaken to Strengthen: Weakening-Induced On-Policy Self-Distillation for Large Reasoning Models","tldr":"WISD improves reasoning models with no labels or stronger teacher by training them toward tokens the original model prefers over a deliberately quantized or pruned copy of itself, adding 4 to 5.5 points on average."},{"id":"2610.34491","date":"2026-10-29","title":"What Effort Level Should I Choose? On the Economics of Reasoning Effort in LLM Agents","tldr":"Across eight models and four benchmarks, higher reasoning effort often loses tasks lower effort solves and costs up to 42x more on easy ones; starting low and escalating on failure does better."},{"id":"2610.33845","date":"2026-10-27","title":"Build, Don't Play: Self-Improving LLM Research Agents Develop a Hearthstone Battlegrounds AI That Rivals Top Players","tldr":"LLM research agents built a faithful Hearthstone Battlegrounds simulator and an RL agent in 20 days; the agent outperformed the server's top-10 players' recent results, while frontier LLMs playing directly fell far short."},{"id":"2610.31778","date":"2026-10-26","title":"Benchmarks Are Surprisingly Compaction-Friendly","tldr":"When long-running coding agents summarize their context to keep going, benchmark scores barely change, but the rules they were given quietly disappear from the summaries."},{"id":"2610.23479","date":"2026-10-24","title":"HexaShell: A Thin Harness for Exploring the Limits of VLM Agents as Robot Coding Agents","tldr":"A stock coding agent drives a simulated two-arm robot through one command line and rewrites small measurement tools after each failure; with no training it reaches 46.9% success on RoboDojo's official evaluation."},{"id":"2610.26828","date":"2026-10-22","title":"Agent World Model in the Wild: Computer-Use Agent Environment Synthesis","tldr":"WildAWM uses open models to synthesize 341 verifiable, long-horizon computer-use tasks across GUI, command line and MCP, and RL on them improves Qwen models on all eight unseen benchmarks."},{"id":"2610.26860","date":"2026-10-21","title":"OpenVLHarness: Real World Visual Agentic Tool-Use with Multimodal Memory","tldr":"OpenVLHarness gives vision-language models typed tools plus a persistent artifact memory, lifting 22-benchmark averages by 9.7 to 12.6 points and beating maximum-effort reasoning at no more than 37% of the tokens."}]}